window.WIKI_ENTRY={"id": "concept-005", "name_zh": "梦宇宙", "name_en": "Dream universe", "tagline": "赛斯说的「梦宇宙」不是你醒来就忘掉的幻影，而是一个和物质宇宙一样真实、有分子结构、由心灵感应黏合的持续实相——你每夜都在里面活动、创造，它也在反过来滋养你的物质生活。", "explanation": "梦宇宙是赛斯早期课里反复讲的一个「第二实相」：它和你们熟知的物理宇宙一样真实、一样有凝聚力，靠同一种心灵感应黏合，由分子构成却不占你们所知的空间。你不是「做了个梦」就完事——你在梦宇宙里持续地创造、活动，你的梦反过来也影响物质世界，两个场域不断互相补给能量。它还是人格的一部分（你的人格在梦里也有实相），也是物质宇宙能存在的条件之一；没有它，肉身根本无法存在。对赛斯来说，你们的物理世界反倒像是一个他「受邀参观」的梦宇宙。所以梦不是幻影，而是和醒时生活同样真实、同样是「行动本身」的一个舞台。", "definitions": [{"zh": "梦宇宙和你们自己的宇宙一样真实、一样有凝聚力，把它聚合在一起的是同样的心电感应粘合剂。", "en": "the dream universe is as real and cohesive as your own, and that the same glue of telepathy holds it together", "source": "Session 92"}, {"zh": "你创造一个现实，一个梦宇宙，和物质宇宙一样真实。", "en": "You create an actuality, a dream universe, as real as the physical universe.", "source": "Session 127"}, {"zh": "梦宇宙有分子结构，但这种分子结构不占用你们知道的空间。", "en": "The dream universe has molecular construction, but this molecular construction takes up no space as you know it.", "source": "Session 149"}, {"zh": "梦世界是你自身存在的一个副产品。", "en": "the dream world is a by-product of your own existence.", "source": "Session 97"}], "blocks": [{"id": "B01", "title": "梦宇宙到底是什么：和物质宇宙一样真实的另一个系统", "note": "赛斯最先把梦宇宙介绍成一种和你们的物质宇宙「一样真实、一样有凝聚力」的实相，把两者黏在一起的同样是心灵感应（telepathy），不是物理胶水。它不是你们白日想象出来的影子，而是独立存在的——就像存有（entity）扩展出人格、人格再变成独立个体，这些个体也会创造自己的梦实相，以及梦宇宙里独立的个体。梦世界其实是你们自己存在的一个副产品，而且因为是靠化学反应和你们连着的，动物、甚至树都有它们自己的梦，所有实体物质都参与了梦宇宙的非自主建构。研究梦宇宙，反而能帮人看懂物质世界背后那个更基本的内在。判断：这是入门定位——梦宇宙不是幻觉，是与物质宇宙平起平坐的另一个客观系统。", "src": "第92、95、97、109、114、149节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 92 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 95 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 97 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 109 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 114 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 149 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-005-e0001", "zh": "不过，我想强调一点，梦宇宙和你们自己的宇宙一样真实、一样有凝聚力，把它聚合在一起的是同样的心电感应粘合剂 ，不仅仅赋予它一样多的实相，也赋予它实实在在的效力。 [梦境宇宙与你们的宇宙一样真实连贯，同样以心灵感应作为粘合剂，使梦境宇宙拥有同等的真实可信度。 ]", "en": "I want to make a point however, that the dream universe is as real and cohesive as your own, and that the same glue of telepathy holds it together, and gives it not only as much reality but validity in actual terms.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第92节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "92", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0003", "zh": "同一种心灵协议（psychic agreement），就像结合物质宇宙一样结合梦宇宙。如果一个人能够真的聚焦在物质宇宙中人类根本无法同意的隐藏、恐惧、大部分未知、没有组织的元素上；如果他能够聚焦在物质宇宙的相异之处而不是相似之处，他就会怀疑是谁让任何人以为有一个人人都同意的物质宇宙。", "en": "The same sort of psychic agreement holds the dream universe together as holds the physical universe together. If a man could actually focus his concentration upon those hidden, feared, mainly unknown, unrecognized elements in the physical universe upon which men simply cannot agree; if he could focus upon the dissimilarities rather than the similarities in the physical universe, he would wonder what gave anyone the idea that there was even one physical object upon which men could agree.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第92节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "92", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0005", "zh": "但双脚的确会走路，梦宇宙也的确存在。就像存有扩展并创始新的人格，然后这些人格接着变成独立的个体一样，这些个体也创造梦或所谓的梦实相以及梦宇宙的个体，而且他们是独立的。", "en": "But the legs do walk, and the dream universe does exist. As the entity expands and originates new personalities, and these personalities then become independent individuals, so do the individuals create dream or so-called dream realities and individuals of the dream universe, which are independent.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第92节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "92", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0007", "zh": "重要的是，你明白梦世界是你自身存在的一个副产品。因为它和你透过化学反应连结在一起，所以这让互动的入口保持畅通，在动物和人类身上都是。由于梦是任何和物质有关联的意识衍生的一个副产品，因此这带着我们做出正确的结论——树有它们的梦，所有的实体物质，都是由不同程度的意识个体单位形成，也都参与了梦宇宙的非自主性建构。", "en": "It is important that you realize that the dream world is a by-product of your own existence. And because it is connected to you through chemical reactions this leaves open the entryway of interactions, in animals as well as men. Since dreams are a by-product of any consciousness involved with matter, this leads us to the correct conclusion—that trees have their dreams, that all physical matter, being formed about individualized units of consciousness of varying degrees, also participates in the involuntary construction of the dream universe.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第97节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "97", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0010", "zh": "我希望讲讲你们所知的物质宇宙、负物质宇宙以及真正的梦宇宙如何平行发展。", "en": "I would like to speak concerning the parallel development of the universe of matter as you know it, the universe of negative matter, and what is truly the universe of dreams.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第109节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "109", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0011", "zh": "我这里同样不是在标榜直觉胜过理智。它们两者各有不同的目的。它们的频率对准不同的实相，而且所有的实相都是真的。但我们的上一节，以你们能够了解的说法简单解释过发展，这应该让你们明白了，因为梦宇宙和物质宇宙的平行发展，所以研究梦宇宙将帮助你们理解你们居住的物质世界背后那基本的内在。", "en": "I am again, not here praising the intuitions above the intellect. They are both intended for different purposes. They tune in on different realities, and all realities are actual. Nevertheless our last session, with its simplified explanation of development in terms that you can understand, should lead you to realize that because of the parallel development of the dream universe with the physical universe, the study of the dream universe will help you comprehend the basic inwardness behind the physical world that you inhabit.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第109节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "109", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0013", "zh": "物质的具体化如此被建构而成，因而导致内在能量本身进一步的再生。我想要再讲一次，梦一直不断发生，不管你是醒是睡；实情永远都是这样。梦宇宙也影响你们自己的物质宇宙，因为物质宇宙强烈地影响它。", "en": "The physical materialization was so constructed that it resulted in further regeneration of inward energy itself. I would like to repeat that dreams occur constantly, whether you wake or sleep; and this has always been the case. The dream universe has also affected your own physical universe, as the physical universe has strongly affected it.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第109节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "109", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0036", "zh": "梦宇宙和你们自己的宇宙两者都是现实，两者都是互相连结的分开系统。", "en": "The dream universe and your own are both actualities, and both separate systems that are interconnected.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第114节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "114", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0064", "zh": "梦宇宙也不是你们自己的影子意象。它根据它之内本来具有的可能性继续下去，就像你们按照物质场域之内的可能性继续下去一样。不过，在这两个场域之内，行动的可能性会有变化，就像在所有其他场域之内一样。你们可以说，你们在睡觉时聚焦自己的能量，形成了一个不同的实相，而这有别于醒时物质实相。", "en": "Nor is the dream universe a shadow image of your own. It carries on according to the possibilities inherent within it, as you carry on according to the possibilities that exist within the physical field. The possibilities for action vary, however, within these two fields as they vary within all other fields. You may say that in sleeping you focus your energies to form a different reality than the reality of waking physical matter.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第149节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "149", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B02", "title": "梦宇宙和物质宇宙怎么互相喂养：平行发展与双向能量", "note": "梦宇宙和物质宇宙不是各过各的，而是「平行发展」、互相喂养的两个场域。某些象征在梦宇宙里被建构成实相，就跟某些意念在物质宇宙里被建构成物质是同一套机制；反过来，人在物质上搞懂了火、发明了东西，也会让梦宇宙变得更丰富、更自由。两头的能量一直在对流：你们给梦宇宙能量，它也回给你们；看似在物质里「浪费掉」或「用不上」的能量，其实会渗进梦宇宙去保证物质宇宙本身的存在。这是一种施与受——所有场域其实都唇齿相依。判断：这一块讲「互动」，核心就是双向的能量与观念的交换。", "src": "第92、109、115、149、151节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 92 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 109 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 115 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 149 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 151 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-005-e0002", "zh": "所以他们的梦世界在某些方面没有你们以为的那么不同。某些象征在梦宇宙里被建构成实相，所以，用差不多相同的方式，某些意念在物质宇宙里也被建构成物质。", "en": "Their dream worlds are not then so diverse in some ways as you might have supposed. Certain symbols are constructed into realities in the dream universe, then, in much the same manner that certain ideas are constructed into matter in the physical universe.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第92节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "92", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0012", "zh": "所以，梦宇宙和负物质宇宙是物质宇宙的副产品，因为它们是在内在能量试图以物质方式形成它自己之际被形成的。", "en": "Both the dream universe and the universe of negative matter then, are by-products of the physical universe, in that they were formed as inward energy attempted to form itself in a physical way.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第109节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "109", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0014", "zh": "观念、意念，在梦中实现，接着在物质上被建构出来。物质建构和发明，纯粹是就理智上对物质的一个新的理解而言，也转化了梦宇宙的本质，并且让它更丰富，增加那里在象征上可能有的自由。", "en": "Concepts, ideas, realized in dreams, have then been constructed physically. Physical constructions and inventions, purely in terms of a new intellectual comprehension of physical matter, have also transformed the nature of the dream universe, and enriched it, adding to the symbolistic freedoms possible there.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第109节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "109", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0016", "zh": "他在物质上精通用火之后，他在智性上了解到火的好处，于是他的梦宇宙增添了新的自由。这只是其中一个例子而已。虽然两个宇宙的发展从头到尾是平行的，但并不是每一方面都一模一样的平均。也就是说，一个观念可能灿烂地活在梦宇宙里，但在物质上没有被表现出来，或是，基于某个原因，物质宇宙里的一个理智上的理解，可能在梦宇宙里找不到表现方式。但整体而言，发展是平行的。", "en": "With his intellectual appreciation of the benefits of fire that followed his physical mastery of it, then his dream universe became enriched with a new freedom. This is but one simple example. While development of the two universes overall is parallel, no exact evenness in all respects is achieved. That is, a concept may be brilliantly alive in the dream universe but unexpressed physically, or for one reason or another an intellectual comprehension in the physical universe may not find expression in the dream universe. But overall there is parallel development.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第109节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "109", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0021", "zh": "但是看不到意义。没有能量不被使用。熵（Entropy）不存在。它只是在物质视角之内一个效应的表象而已；那股看似无法使用的能量协助形成你的梦宇宙。那股来自你似乎在物质上派不上用场的能量，那股价值似乎减少的能量，被往后犁进内在、再生并用来形成各个宇宙，没有那些宇宙，你们甚至不可能以肉身存在体的方式存在。", "en": "But the significance is not seen. No energy is not used. Entropy does not exist. It is the appearance only of an effect within the physical perspectives; that seemingly unusable energy helps form your dream universe. That energy from which you seem to get no work physically, that energy which seems to diminish in value, is plowed backward into inwardness, regenerated and used to form universes without which you could not exist even as physical beings.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第109节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "109", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0024", "zh": "能量在物质宇宙看似丧失或消散，或是无法使用，事实上的确是离开它；但它自行转移，渗入梦宇宙，在那里协助确保物质宇宙本身的存在，因为这些场域或宇宙的存在每一个都以最实际的方式，仰赖着其他场域或宇宙的存在。", "en": "Energy seemingly lost or dissipated or unusable in the physical universe does indeed leave it; but it transfers itself, seeps into the dream universe, and there it helps to insure the existence of the physical universe itself, since the existence of each of these fields or universes is dependent upon the existence of the others, in most actual ways.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第109节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "109", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0039", "zh": "你们的确给它们能量，就像它们也给你们能量。梦，或梦宇宙，甚至在你们醒时都存在，甚至在你们睡着时也只有觉察到它的某些部分而已。你们确实创造它，但它到某种程度也独立于你们之外。在你们的自我体验它和物质世界之间关系里种种的变化之际，你们也据此改变梦世界的种种面向，并让它更丰富。", "en": "You do indeed give them energy, as they also give you energy. Dreams, or the dream universe, exists even while you wake, and you only become aware of certain portions of it even while you sleep. You do create it, but it is also to some degree independent of you. As your ego experiences changes in its relationship with the physical world, so do you change aspects of the dream world accordingly, and enrich it.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第115节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "115", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0046", "zh": "因此，可以说，在很多方面梦宇宙依赖你们来给它表达方式，同样的，你们也依赖它来找到表达方式，但是在这个情况中，你有其他的出口，而它有的很少。任何一个梦的冲击都有物质、化学、电磁、心理和心灵的反射。这些也是实际而且持续的，它们不仅代表在所有这些情况中你的一部分环境，也深深影响日常生活的一般管道。", "en": "It might be said then, that in many ways the dream universe depends upon you to give it expression, in the same manner that you also depend upon it to find expression, although in this case you have other outlets, and it has few. The impact of any given dream has physical, chemical, electromagnetic, psychological and psychic repercussions. These are also actual and continuing, and they not only represent a part of your environment in all of these cases, but they affect most deeply the ordinary channels of everyday life.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第115节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "115", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0063", "zh": "我说过，我所谓的梦宇宙事实上是由分子结构组成，那是一种连续不断的实相，即使你们基于非常必要的理由，经常只将它局限在自己的睡眠期间里。这里有一种施与受，因为如果你们赋于梦宇宙很多它自己连绵不绝的能量，就能从梦里获得很多你们自己的能量。物质场域和梦宇宙两者相互依赖，这种现象一点都不足为奇，因为所有场域实际上都是唇齿相依。", "en": "I have mentioned that what I call the dream universe is indeed composed of molecular structure, and that it is a continuing reality, even though your own awareness of it is most usually limited, for quite necessary reasons, to the hours of your own sleep. There is a give and take here, for if you give the dream universe much of its continuing energy, much of your own energy is derived from it. There is, between the physical field and the dream universe, an interdependence that is not at all unusual, for all fields are indeed dependent one upon the other.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第149节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "149", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0077", "zh": "我提过你们的宇宙和梦宇宙之间的化学关系，有某种类似的关系，把所有场域和系统绑在一起，从最大的到最小的。内我的自由从来不是由你们所知的时间决定，而是由你们不知道的时间决定。", "en": "I mentioned the chemical relationship between your universe and the dream universe. There are like relationships of one kind or another that tie together all fields and systems, from the largest to the most minute. The freedom of the inner self, then, is never determined by time as you know it. It is determined by time as you do not know it.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第151节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "151", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B03", "title": "梦宇宙是怎么搭起来的：分子结构、不占空间、时间不重要", "note": "梦宇宙虽然是「由分子组成」，但这些分子不占你们所知的空间，它靠的是深度、维度、扩张与收缩，更接近一种不必套用物质结构的理想。时间在这里几乎不算数——这也是它不像物质宇宙那样需要永久意象的原因；在这里直觉和内在能力自由得多，价值完成（value fulfillment）被放开了手脚，所以行动更自发、更流畅，意象生灭更快。它并非没有结构，而是结构属于心智或心灵的层次，不依赖物质。你在物质里体验的「一瞬间」，在梦里可能装着几乎难以置信的经验深度。判断：这块讲「构造」，要破除的是「梦是一团乱、很虚」的错觉。", "src": "第109、149、162、188节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 109 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 149 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 162 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 188 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-005-e0020", "zh": "不用说也知道，或应该知道，内我透过物质宇宙和梦宇宙两者发送它内在感官的投射；不过这一番讲到空间和配置的话，只不过为了方便而已。然而，就物质建构而言，你会发现的就是这个，而且，如果可以理解的话，在你们的实验室里进行观察，就会在最微小物质粒子的实际建构中看到这个。", "en": "It goes without saying, or should, that the inner self sends its projections of inner senses through both the physical universe and the dream universe; yet all this talk of space and placement is a mere convenience. Yet, in terms of physical construction this is what you would find, and this, if it were understood, is what is seen in the actual construction of the most minute physical particle under observation in your laboratories.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第109节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "109", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0069", "zh": "梦宇宙有分子结构，但这种分子结构不占用你们知道的空间。梦宇宙虽然是由分子组成，但不是由你们所知的物质组成。梦宇宙是由种种深度与维度、扩展与收缩组成，或许更加接近完美的理想，而不必透过你们所熟悉的那种特定结构。", "en": "The dream universe has molecular construction, but this molecular construction takes up no space as you know it. The dream universe, while composed of molecules, is not composed of matter as you know it. The dream universe consists of depths and dimensions, expansions and contractions, that are more clearly allied, perhaps, to ideals that have no need for the particular kind of structure with which you are familiar.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第149节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "149", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0070", "zh": "从连续性的角度来看，在梦宇宙里，时间显然不是一个重要元素，而这也是梦宇宙里没有物质结构的原因之一。这里直觉和某些内在能力的自由度高很多，所以不需要以任何禁锢的形式或结构使用分子。在梦宇宙之内，行动更自发、更流畅。意象的出现与消失也快很多，因为价值完成被赋予更大的支配权。", "en": "Obviously, time in terms of continuity, is not an element of importance in the dream universe, and this is one of the reasons for the lack of physical structure. The intuitions and certain inner abilities here have so much more freedom that it is unnecessary for molecules to be used in any imprisoning form or structure. Action is more spontaneous within the dream universe, more fluid. The images appear and disappear much more quickly because value fulfillment is allowed greater reign.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第149节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "149", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0071", "zh": "不过，在梦宇宙里，较为缓慢的物质成长过程被心灵和心智的价值完成取代，而没有必要把分子长期囚禁在模式之内。", "en": "In the dream universe however the slower physical growth process is replaced by psychic and mental value fulfillment, which does not necessitate any long-range imprisonment of molecules within a pattern.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第149节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "149", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0072", "zh": "这只不过是经验和行动的加速而已，相对来说，不受物质宇宙内那种对时间的固有需求所阻碍，因此行动本身得以拥有较大的自由。这不是说在梦宇宙之内没有结构的存在，因为一种心智或心灵性质的结构的确存在。但结构不像在物质宇宙里那样依赖物质，而且分子的带动更为自发，同时，在你们看似一瞬之间的片刻之内，可能就存在着一种几乎令人无法置信的经验深度。", "en": "This involves, simply, a quickening of experience and action relatively unhampered by the sort of time necessities inherent within the physical universe. Action itself therefore is allowed greater freedom. This is not to say that structure does not exist within the dream universe, for structures of a mental or psychic nature do exist. But structure is not dependent upon matter as in the physical universe, and the motion of molecules is more spontaneous, and an almost unbelievable depth of experience is possible within what would seem to you a fraction of a moment.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第149节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "149", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0073", "zh": "有关这两个场域之间的连结以及它们在行动上的显现，我还有更多要说，因为你们对纯粹的行动最为贴近的一瞥，其中之一就是在梦宇宙之内的行动，以及人格进出梦领域时的那种机动性。在你们自己的宇宙里，你们所做的事是将行动转化为物质操纵，但这只是行动的一小部分而已，而我的目的是要让你们对于行动的原始真实面目有一些认识。", "en": "I will have more to say concerning the connection between the two fields and their manifestation in action, for one of the closest glimpses you can get of pure action is action as it is involved within the dream universe, and in this mobility as the personality passes into and out of the dream field. Within your own universe you deal with the transformation of action into physical manipulations, but this involves but a small portion of the nature of action, and it is my purpose to familiarize you with action as it exists more or less in its pure form.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第149节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "149", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0074", "zh": "梦世界或梦宇宙的整体实相大致就是这样。不过，在它之内实现和发展并不依赖实体物质的恒久性，也完全不依赖任何类似你们物理时间的概念。因此，在未被时间束缚的视角之内，时机一成熟，对醒时的自己而言，可能就会出现爆炸性的发展。", "en": "The whole reality of the dream world, or of the dream universe, lies along these lines. Within it fulfillment and development are not dependent upon permanence of physical matter, however, and are not at all dependent upon any concept like that of your physical time. There [are] therefore possible bursts of developments, that have matured within perspectives that are not bound up in time, and that would appear spontaneous to the waking self.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第149节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "149", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0082", "zh": "就如同你们不知不觉中持续创造实体物质一样，你们也持续在创造梦宇宙。这个梦宇宙跟你们物质场域中的环境一样具有个别性，这里也会有化学反应，因为没有了梦，物质组织也无法存在。 你们运用外在感官所能感知到的，只不过是伪装的物质实相而已，因为肉体感官本来就是来感知物质实相。但是在梦宇宙里，你们在空间和时间上却可以运用自由且熟悉的方式，而这样的方式你们在醒时状态却拒绝使用。你们梦境中的地点到底在哪里？梦里你们走过的那条街，究竟位于空间中的什么地方？", "en": "As you create physical matter constantly without knowing that you do so, so also you create constantly a dream universe, and this dream universe is as individual as your environment in the physical world. There is also a chemical reaction here, for without dreaming the physical organism could not exist. With your outer senses, you perceive but the camouflage physical reality which the physical senses are equipped to perceive. In the dream universe you are however free, and familiar, with both space and time in a manner which is denied you in the waking state. Where indeed are your dream locations? Where in space is the street upon which you walk in a dream?", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第162节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "162", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0100", "zh": "梦影像，非灵体投射，在动作时受到某些电子上的限制，这些限制形成了梦宇宙的界限。然而，梦影像几乎都是类似纤维状的投射，是一种近乎稀稀疏疏的组合结构，基本上来说，它们比实体物质还具有可塑性，不过是由许多相同的属性所组成。再说一次，梦的本质与物质实相的东西，两者间必定有这种连结。", "en": "Dream images, not astral projections, operate within certain electrical limits, limits that form the boundaries of the dream universe. Dream images are nevertheless almost fibrous projections, almost a thinned-out composition, more plastic basically than physical matter, but composed of a number of the same properties. For again there must be this connection between the nature of dreams and the matter of physical reality.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第188节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "188", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B04", "title": "梦宇宙和「人格」有什么关系：人格在梦里也有实相", "note": "在赛斯体系里，人格不是一个只在醒时、只在物质里活动的东西——人格在梦宇宙里也有它自己的实相。人格由能量完形构成，所以它造出来的梦可以看成「正在变动中的人格」的一部分；任何经验或行动都会改变人格，梦也一样会改人格。人格的稳定性，某种程度上就取决于它能不能有效操控自己的梦境——人在物质宇宙里操控大家都知道，但在梦宇宙里也要做类似的操控，这点却普遍没人接受。你在梦里会遇见自己的其他部分，而梦宇宙里的经验，在每一方面都和醒时经验一样鲜明、一样真实。判断：这块把梦宇宙接回「人格」这个主概念——它既是人格的舞台，也是人格的组成部分。", "src": "第95、146、162、165、173节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 95 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 146 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 162 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 165 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 173 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-005-e0006", "zh": "现在。我说过你们任何人还有你们所有人都创造一个有效、实际又耐久的梦宇宙，而且为了菲利普好，具有自我决定权（self-determination），方式和存有投射它各个不同人格的实相一样。就像存有与平常有意识的自我之间没有任何接触，那做梦的自己与那有它自己独立存在的梦世界，在有意识的层次上也一样没有任何接触。", "en": "Now. I have said that any of you and all of you create a dream universe of validity, actuality, durability, and for Philip's benefit, self-determination, in the same manner that the entity projects the reality of its various personalities. As there is no contact between the entity and the ordinary conscious ego, so there is no contact on a conscious level between the self who dreams and the dream world which has its own independent existence.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第95节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "95", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0091", "zh": "你们探索某个系统时，必定会影响到其他系统。将人格视为与组成它的那些同时存在的行动分开，基本上没什么意义，如你们所知，人格在梦宇宙之内也有一个实相。然而，以最基本也最实际的方式，人格显然与物理时间毫无牵连。只有一部分的人格，也就是自我，跟物理时间深深牵连。显而易见的是，那些对自我来说，在时间上似乎已摇不可及的刺激，人格系统却会对它们起反应。换言之，就自我的时间概念而言，一个发生在20年前的刺激，人格可以在当下对它起反应。", "en": "You cannot probe into the one system without affecting the others. It is basically meaningless to consider the personality as separate from the simultaneous actions of which it is composed. The personality, as you know, has also a reality within the dream universe. It should be obvious that in a most basic and practical manner the personality however is not involved with physical time to any degree. Only a part of the personality, the ego, is so involved. It is obvious of course that the personality system will react to stimuli that seem, to the ego, to be far divorced in time. That is, the personality may react to a stimuli in the present that occurred originally twenty years ago, to the ego's understanding of time.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第165节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "165", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0094", "zh": "这个主题我们之前已讨论了一些，但还没有深入探究过，现在该是我们付诸行动的时候。如你们所知，人格由能量完形构成，因此人格所创造的梦可以当成是变动中人格的一部分。我们现在仅就单一背景来说，因为我们知道，梦宇宙多多少少也独立于人格之外。", "en": "We have discussed this subject to some degree. However we have not begun a study in depth. It is now time for us to do so. The personality as you know is composed of energy gestalts. The dreams created by the personality can be considered therefore as a part of the changing personality. We are speaking here in one context only, for we know that the dream universe is also to some extent independent of personality.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第173节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "173", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0095", "zh": "在这个独特的背景下，可以来思考梦世界与人格之间的关系。从很多方面来看，梦宇宙确实会在这种背景下运作，而且也是人格架构的一部分。任何经验或行动都会改变人格，所以人格也会被它自己的梦改变。这里我们再度看到了能量或行动如何在它本身里面运作，我们甚至可以追踪这些行动和互动的状况。", "en": "In this particular context however the dream world will be considered in its relationship to the personality. In many ways the dream universe does operate within this context, and is part of the personality framework. As the personality is changed by any experience or any action, so it is changed by its own dreams. Here again we see how energy or action operates within itself. We can even trace the actions and interactions.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第173节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "173", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0096", "zh": "梦宇宙对内我的真实性，就跟物质宇宙对意识自我（the conscious egotistical self）的真实性完全一样，这一点不用多说。物质宇宙对内我相对不重要，就如梦宇宙对意识自我也比较不重要一样。", "en": "It goes without saying that the dream universe is every bit as real to the inner self as the physical universe is to the conscious egotistical self. The physical universe is relatively （underline relatively） as unimportant to the inner self as the dream universe appears to be to the egotistical self.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第173节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "173", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0097", "zh": "它一直都在这个架构里面，但并不是永远都在里面维持同样的相对位置。人格的稳定性或多或少取决于它掌握或操控这些梦境的效能。人格会在物质宇宙之内操控，这一点众所周知，不过人格在梦宇宙之内也一定会做类似的操控，这一点大家普遍都不知道。", "en": "It is always within this framework, but not always does it maintain the same relative position within it. The stability of the personality depends in some degree upon the effectiveness with which it handles and manipulates these dream situations. It is realized that the personality manipulates within the physical universe, but the fact is not generally accepted that similar manipulations must be made within this dream universe.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第173节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "173", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0086", "zh": "自我没办法让心脏跳动。你们在梦中遇见其他部分的自己，那为什么你们还很难相信自我只是你们的一部分，自我无法代表全部呢？你们建构各种实相，对于意识上被你们忽略的梦宇宙，你们其实并不陌生。你们在梦宇宙里的经验，各方面都跟你们醒时经验一样鲜明、一样确切、也一样真实。", "en": "The ego cannot make your heart beat. Why then do you find it difficult to believe that you are more than the ego, for in dreams you meet portions of yourself. You construct realities, and you are indeed familiar with the dream universe that consciously you ignore. And your experience within the dream universe is as vivid and as valid and as real, in every respect, as your waking experience.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第162节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "162", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0062", "zh": "可以说，自己被扩展，存在很多维度之内。它在梦宇宙之中，就像它在你们自己的物质宇宙之中一样，都斩钉截铁般实际地扩展。它是电子宇宙的一部分，就如同它是心理动机的一部分一样，在四面八方无止尽地交织着。", "en": "The self is extended, so to speak, existing within many dimensions. It extends as vitally and actually in the dream universe as it does in your own physical universe. It is as much a part of the electrical universe as it is a part of the world of psychological motivation. The intertwinings are infinite in all directions.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第146节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "146", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B05", "title": "能不能主动进去「收听」梦宇宙：门户与醒时做梦", "note": "既然梦宇宙是真实系统，那能不能「主动」进去收听？赛斯说可以：睡眠时在做，所谓的醒时状态也能做。进入的门户有三种——化学的、电子的、心理的——三者必须同时打开，但任意一个被打开会顺带打开另外两个；它们醒时不常开，一旦喀嚓开启，通常借由一次暂时的化学失衡，肉身就同时连上了梦宇宙和物质宇宙。梦本身是通过电子模式被直接感知、再解码的，原始经验是电子性的。你日夜都在造梦宇宙（在潜意识基础上），而且没有梦，肉身组织根本活不了。判断：这块给读者「怎么接触它」——门户、收听、以及醒时做梦这件事。", "src": "第118、123、126、162、193节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 118 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 123 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 126 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 162 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 193 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-005-e0048", "zh": "我们从上一节以来留下很多尚未了结的问题。我跟你们讲过，收听梦宇宙是可能的。你知道这是在睡眠期间做的事。它也可以在所谓的醒时状态做。", "en": "We have left many loose ends since our last session. I have told you that it is possible to tune in on the dream universe. You know this is done during sleep. It can also be done in the so-called waking state.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第118节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "118", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0049", "zh": "它们有几个的确和收听梦宇宙有关。有很多电台，可以这样说，收听梦宇宙，目前你们相当不加选择地转动电台旋扭。各种现实层面处处存在。我说的的确是这个意思。外太空表面的空无，一点都不空无，但这些不一定是你用想像所及最先进的太空船能够一探究竟的世界。", "en": "A few of them did involve a tuning into the dream universe. There are many stations, so to speak, to tune into, and at present you touch the dials rather indiscriminately. Planes of actuality of one sort or another everywhere exist. I mean that literally. The apparent emptiness of outer space is far from empty, but these are not necessarily worlds that you could visit with the most advanced imaginable spaceship.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第118节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "118", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0051", "zh": "我们也务必理清其他主题的一些重点。我们不久就会比较直接讨论到个别的梦。要进行这样的讨论必须先打好坚固的基础。进入梦宇宙有各个不同的门户：化学门户、电子门户，以及心理门户。这三个必须全部一口气打开，也就是同时，但是任何一个门都会自动打开另外两个。", "en": "We must also clear up some points on other topics. We will shortly be concerned more directly with discussions of individual dreams. It is necessary that a firm ground be prepared for such discussion. There are various doorways into the dream universe: chemical doorways, electronic doorways, and psychological doorways. All three must be opened at once, that is simultaneously, but any one door will automatically open the others.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第118节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "118", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0052", "zh": "它们在醒时状态不常打开。当它们喀嚓一声开启时，通常但并不总是在化学上透过暂时的不平衡，物质有机体本身和梦宇宙，也和你们的物质宇宙连结上；而且到某种程度，可以透过这个连结影响物质有机体。", "en": "They open infrequently in the waking state. When they are clicked open, usually but not always chemically through a momentary imbalance, the physical organism itself is connected to the dream universe, as well as to your physical universe; and to some degree the physical organism can be affected through this connection.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第118节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "118", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0053", "zh": "透过电子模式直接感知梦，然后解码。最初的经验，因此，再说一次，是一个电子经验，而且依据最初的电荷强度，人类系统立刻感觉到它的效应。在梦宇宙这方面，我没有讲很多，因为首先你们必须了解情感和思想的电子现实。不久之后在这个主题上我会谈更多。", "en": "Dreams are felt directly through electrical patterns, and then decoded. The original experience, then, again, is an electric one, and the effects are instantly felt by the human system, according to the original intensity of the charge. I have not spoken much concerning the dream universe, since first it was necessary that you understand the electrical actuality of emotions and thoughts. I shall have more to say on this subject shortly.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第123节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "123", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0081", "zh": "再说一次，你们是在潜意识的基础上建构梦宇宙，梦宇宙是以它自己的方式，跟物质一样耐久。你们不论醒时或睡时都会做梦，你们只有在睡觉时才熟悉你们的梦，因为在那里你们的感知和能量才会聚焦在那个方向。", "en": "You construct the dream universe, again, on a subconscious basis. The dream universe is as permanent in its way as the physical universe. You construct dreams whether you wake or you sleep. You are only familiar with your dreams when you sleep, for then your perception and your energy is focused in that direction.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第162节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "162", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0083", "zh": "你在梦中可能经验了两、三个钟头，但在物理时间只是一瞬间，你并没有因此老了两三个钟头。梦宇宙里面所经验的时间和空间，非常接近内我纯然的样貌。在这里，自己摆脱了自我，因而就不需要将意念建构到物质实相中。", "en": "You may in a dream experience two or three hours in a flash of physical time. You have not aged two or three hours. The experience of space and time within the dream universe comes very close to the pure expression of the inner self. For here, free from the ego, the self is relieved of the necessity of constructing ideas into physical reality.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第162节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "162", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0101", "zh": "因此这类主观的事件，会透过经验它们的人格来操纵实体物质。对任何人格而言，实相的领域必须也确实包含了所有这些活动的领域，因为它们为他的存在提供了形式和维度。我之前提过，除非个体也同时存在于梦宇宙，否则他无法存在于物质宇宙。再说一次，在所有这些意识状况之间，有一些化学和电磁上的连结无法切割。", "en": "Such subjective events therefore manipulate physical matter through the personality who experiences them. The field of reality for any given personality must and does include all these areas of activity, for they give form and dimension to his existence. I have said earlier that the individual could not exist in a physical universe if he did not also exist in the dream universe. Again, there are chemical and electromagnetic connections that cannot be severed between all these states of consciousness.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第193节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "193", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0054", "zh": "这些影响全部都在肉身个体的成形当中扮演一个角色，他的存在也仰赖一种平衡的维持。在某些情况当中，打个比喻，力量的强度累积，严重的短路的确会发生。比方说，梦宇宙可能带着不寻常的鲜明度入侵。系统们失去互补的平衡，但整体而言，系统们非常有效率地在一起运作。", "en": "All of these influences have a part in the formation of the physical individual, and his existence is dependent upon a balance being maintained. In some instances, to use an analogy, serious short circuits do occur, intensities of power accumulate. The dream universe, for example, may intrude with unusual sharpness. The systems lose complementary balance, but on the whole the systems operate together most efficiently.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第126节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "126", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B06", "title": "梦宇宙凭什么是「创造源头」：负物质、转化与神圣心理苗床", "note": "梦宇宙不只是平行系统，它还是物质宇宙能存在的条件之一——没有它，你们在物质上根本无法存在。它是物质宇宙和负物质宇宙二者的副产品（内在能量试图以物质方式形成自己时被挤出来的），而梦宇宙自己的副产品则是负物质世界。它也是「转化」发生的场域：很多在物质里实现不了的宏大观念先在梦宇宙里活着，有一天会反过来转变物质场域的历史；像基督升天这种事，在赛斯看来就是梦宇宙对你们宇宙的一次贡献。放到最大尺度，赛斯甚至说所有宇宙都跃自一个「基本的梦宇宙」——一个神圣的心理苗床，主观存在被自己无限的创造欲点燃，想象物变成了世界。判断：这块把梦宇宙抬到「创造源头」的层级。", "src": "第109、115、897节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 109 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 115 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 897 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-005-e0022", "zh": "因为没有梦宇宙，你们在物质上就无法存在。我很快会开始谈负物质宇宙，但简短说一下，只是为了让你们明白存在具有的相互交织性质；也让你们了解我们在讨论中将会如何跟随它。", "en": "For without the dream universe you could not exist physically. I am going to quickly embark into the universe of negative matter, but briefly, only to show you the interwoven quality of existence; and how we will follow it in discussion.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第109节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "109", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0023", "zh": "一个封闭的系统可能变成，可以说，被还在扩展的其他系统捕获，并用来当作积木，但仍保有它的个体性。以这样的方式，你们的物质宇宙、梦宇宙和负宇宙聚合在一起，又同时保有它们或多或少是一个封闭系统的疆界。 你们必须理解我是为了简化才这样说，因为没有一个系统是完全封闭的。现在。真要开始讨论起它的副产品，我们谈梦宇宙根本谈得不够多。可是呢，我要告诉你们，它的副产品就是负物质世界。", "en": "A closed system could become captured, so to speak, and be used as a building block, still retaining its individuality, by other systems still expanding. In this manner your physical universe, dream universe, and universe of negative matter have come together, while retaining their boundaries as a more or less closed system. You will have to understand that I speak for simplicity’s sake, since no system is completely closed. Now. We have not said nearly enough about the dream universe, to really launch a discussion concerning its by-product. Nevertheless I shall tell you that its by-product is the world of negative matter.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第109节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "109", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0025", "zh": "这股能量接着在梦宇宙转化，再一次再生，并从梦宇宙渗入，用来形成负物质宇宙。我们的讨论必须要先彻底探究梦宇宙的本质，然后才有希望考量到负物质宇宙，但是，如果你把上面提到的事实记在心里也无妨。", "en": "The energy is then transformed in the dream universe, and again regenerated and used in the formation of the universe of negative matter, into which it seeps from the dream universe. Our discussions will have to thoroughly discuss the nature of the dream universe before we can hope to consider the universe of negative matter, but it will not hurt if you keep the above mentioned facts in mind.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第109节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "109", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0040", "zh": "梦宇宙也丰富你们自己的存在。可以这么说，这里有着极大的相互影响，和一种持续的能量交流，而且是透过它们不断经过场域之间而被转化和充电的能量。梦，也许比任何别的东西还要清楚，可以帮助你们了解价值完成，以及不占空间的扩展观念。", "en": "The dream universe also enriches your own existence. There is great interplay here, and a continual interchange of energies, and of energies that are transformed and recharged, so to speak, through their constant passage between fields. Dreams, perhaps more clearly than anything else, can help you understand the concept of value fulfillment, and of the expansion that does not take up space.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第115节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "115", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0041", "zh": "钉十字架是转化和丰富梦宇宙和物质宇宙两者的巨大实相之一，它源自于梦宇宙。它是那个场域对你们自己场域做出的一个主要贡献，在物质上可以比作一颗新的行星在物质宇宙之内的现身。", "en": "The Crucifixion was one of the gigantic realities that transformed and enriched both the universe of dreams and the universe of matter, and it originated in the universe of dreams. It was a main contribution of that field to your own, and could be compared physically to an emergence of a new planet within the physical universe.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第115节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "115", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0043", "zh": "基督升天不是发生在你们知道的时间。它是梦宇宙对你们自己宇宙做出的一个贡献，重现梦宇宙之内人类根本上独立于物质之外的知晓。", "en": "The ascension of Christ did not occur in time as you know it. It is a contribution of the universe of dreams to your own universe, representing knowledge within the dream universe that man was independent of physical matter ultimately.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第115节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "115", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0045", "zh": "这些实相，因为它们在你们系统之内持续不断的效应，以及它们对它的实际转化，应该被彻底研究，因为这样可能有很多收获。相似的转化是事件在你们宇宙之内对梦宇宙做的。往往，再一次，梦宇宙拥有种种观念，有一天，将会完全转变你们场域的历史；但是否认这类观念在实相之内的现实性或可能性，阻碍了这些转化，也拖延了亟需的突破。", "en": "These realities, because of their continuing effects within your system, and their actual transformation of it, should be studied thoroughly, for much can be gained in this way. Like transformations are made by events in your universe upon the dream universe. Often, again, the dream universe possesses concepts which will, some day, completely transform the history of your field; but a denial of such concepts as actualities or possibilities within reality, hold these back, and put off breakthroughs that are sorely needed.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第115节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "115", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0111", "zh": "以一种说法，你们的宇宙及所有其它的宇宙跃自一个次元，那是所有实相的创造源头——可以说，一个基本的梦宇宙，一个神圣的心理苗床。从那儿，主观性的存在被它自己想创造的无限欲望所点燃、光照、刺激及穿透。其力量的源泉是如此之大，而使其想象物变成了世界。但它被赋予了如此光辉灿烂的一个创造力，以致它寻求最精致的完成，因为即使它最微小的思维及它所有的潜力，都被一个真的超过所有想象力的善良意图所引导。", "en": "In a manner of speaking, your universe and all others spring from a dimension that is the creative source for all realities—a basic dream universe, so to speak, a divine psychological bed where subjective being is sparked, illuminated, stimulated, pierced, by its own infinite desire for creativity. The source of its power is so great that its imaginings become worlds, but it is endowed with a creativity of such splendor that it seeks the finest fulfillment, for even the smallest of its thoughts and all of its potentials are directed with a good intent that is literally beyond all imagining.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第897节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "897", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B07", "title": "梦到底真不真：做着梦时它比醒时还生动", "note": "很多人以为梦「不真」，赛斯反复纠正：做着梦的那一刻，做梦者并不觉得虚幻，有些梦比醒时经验更鲜明生动；只有等人格离开梦经验、注意力又回到物质宇宙之后，回头看才觉得梦「好像不真实」。所以实相本质上是能量与注意力聚焦的结果。梦宇宙和物质宇宙一样「客观」，里面的物件和象征是梦中生活忠实的代言，就像物理物件之于醒时生活。你创造的梦宇宙和物质宇宙一样真实，而且像思想、情感一样独立于你之外存在——你影响它，却没法在创造之后叫停一段梦经验。判断：这块是给「梦到底真不真」这个新手最常问的问题一个直接回答。", "src": "第92、109、127、149、259、571节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 92 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 109 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 127 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 149 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 259 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 571 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-005-e0018", "zh": "因此为了简便，我要你们想像，梦宇宙在物质宇宙的另一面占有一个位置，藉由物质把这个实体（entity）从梦宇宙分开来。你们明白了吗？", "en": "So for simplicity’s sake I will have you imagine that the dream universe occupies a position on the other side of the physical universe, with the entity separated from the dream universe by the physical. Do you see?", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第109节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "109", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0066", "zh": "在很多方面，梦宇宙之内的行动，确实都比在你们自己的宇宙里更为直接。梦看起来有时候混乱或无意义，那是由于你们只记得浮光掠影的画面和支离破碎的情节，对自我来讲更是如此，因为自我严格审查很多潜意识保留下来的讯息。", "en": "In many respects actions within the dream universe are indeed more direct than in your own. It is because you remember but vague glimmerings and disconnected episodes that dreams appear, sometimes, chaotic or meaningless, particularly to the ego, which censors rigidly much of the information that the subconscious does retain.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第149节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "149", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0067", "zh": "做梦的人在参与梦经验时，不会觉得虚幻不实，那时候感觉经验是真的，而且有些梦的确比醒时经验更为鲜明生动。只有在人格离开梦经验或梦宇宙后再去回想时，才可能感觉梦经验不真实，因为这时候的注意力和能量的焦点又再度回到物质宇宙中。所以说，实相是能量与注意力聚焦的结果。", "en": "The feeling of unreality is not felt when the dream experience is being participated in by the dreamer. At that time the experience is felt to be real, and some dreams indeed are more vivid than waking experience. It is only when the personality passes out of the dream experience, or the dream universe, that the dream experience in retrospect may appear unreal. For now, again, the focus of attention and energy is in the physical universe. Reality then is a result of the focus of energy and attention.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第149节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "149", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0068", "zh": "我故意用“脱离”梦宇宙这个字眼，因为这里我们很容易看到行动的一种机动性，而且往往已经完成，一种进进出出，涉及到不用在空间之内移动的行动。做梦的人对这种状况很熟悉，也记得自己先前的梦经验，甚至可以说是了如指掌，而且在他的梦行动背后带着很多个人内在的目的。", "en": "I used the term “pass out of” the dream universe purposely, for here we see a mobility of action easily and often accomplished, a passing in and out that involves an action without movement in space. The dreamer is acquainted intimately, and has at his fingertips so to speak, a memory of his previous dream experiences, and carries within him the many inner individualistic purposes which are behind his dream actions.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第149节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "149", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0103", "zh": "你处于这个发展的早期阶段，但它会来的。在梦宇宙之内的这些实相可能是你创造的，但它们和你吃的蛋糕，或你可能吞下的毒药一样真实。就像你的常识在物质宇宙中保护着你一样，在你进行梦物件的操纵时，也必须慎重斟酌。", "en": "You are at the early stages of this development, but it will come. These realities within the dream universe may be created by you, but they are as actual as the piece of cake that you eat, or the poison that you may swallow. As your common sense protects you in the physical universe, so you must use discretion as you progress into the manipulation of dream objects.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第259节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "259", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0108", "zh": "表面上看来非属稳定的“心理物体”在某个层面的梦中环境出现。那么，在物质世界和梦境的两种情形里，象征都遵循法则。如我先前说过的，再说一次，梦的宇宙与物质宇宙是同样的“客观”，在其中的物体与象征是梦中生活的同样忠实的代表，就如物体之于醒时生活一样。", "en": "Seemingly nonstable mental objects appear in the dream environment at certain levels. The symbols follow rules then in both cases. As mentioned earlier, again, the dream universe is as “objective” as the corporeal one. The objects and symbols within it are as faithful representations of dream life as physical objects are of waking life.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第571节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "571", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0004", "zh": "意识心智甚至不知道，而且它本身也无法指挥，双脚走过地板。那么，意识心不知道它怎么创造梦宇宙，又有什么可以觉得奇怪的呢？", "en": "The conscious mind does not even know, and cannot of itself command, the legs to walk across the floor. Is it any wonder, then, that the conscious mind does not know how it creates the dream universe?", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第92节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "92", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0055", "zh": "我告诉过你们，你创造你的梦，在现实里，而不光是在理论中。你创造一个现实，一个梦宇宙，和物质宇宙一样真实。它完全无法在物质宇宙里被感知。互动一直都在。你可以感知梦经验，你可以接收它特定的强度，因为你在那些强度的宇宙之内创造了梦经验。但是梦宇宙和梦经验，就像思想和情感，独立于你之外存在。你影响梦宇宙，但你无法在创造它之后停止一个梦经验，而且你必须在它的存在所能取得的小小强度范围之内创造它，因为没有其他的强度条件或合适的范围能够让这个梦经验存在其中。", "en": "I have told you that you create your dreams, in actuality, not in theory alone. You create an actuality, a dream universe, as real as the physical universe. It simply cannot be directly perceived within the physical universe. There is always interaction. You can perceive the dream experience, you can receive its particular intensities, because you have created the dream experience within the universe of those intensities. But the dream universe and the dream experience, like thoughts and emotions, are independent of you in existence. You influence the dream universe but you cannot stop a dream experience after you have created it, and you must create it within the small range of intensities available for its existence, for there are no other conditions or agreeable ranges of intensity within which the dream experience can exist.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第127节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "127", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B08", "title": "把镜头拉远：梦宇宙和一切实相怎么互相依存", "note": "把镜头再拉远：梦宇宙不是孤零零悬在你们宇宙之外，它和物质宇宙同时在场、互相渗透，两者之间没有真正的界线，任何表面上的分界只是注意力焦点不同造成的。它熟悉你们宇宙的程度，至少不下于你们熟悉它；你们的存活依赖它的存活，它也把频率对准你们。更大一层，梦宇宙还向外延伸到「那些居民」——他们又做着自己的梦、形成电磁实相；整个自己会拿自己在物质实相和梦实相里的各种表现互相比对、自己下结论。就连赛斯自己都说，对「他」而言，你们的世界就是一个他受邀参观、觉得独特又亲切的「梦宇宙」（一个可能的实相）。判断：这块收尾，把梦宇宙放进整张「一切互相依存、没有封闭系统」的网里。", "src": "第108、111、127、146、446、453、560、790节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 108 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 111 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 127 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 146 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 446 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 453 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 560 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 790 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-005-e0008", "zh": "在某些重要的方面，我们会发现即使是当时开始的梦宇宙，和物质宇宙也有一点相同的关系，但在心灵层次上，却是物质宇宙和负物质宇宙有这种关系。它们代表层层表皮、表皮各层，全都属于同一个水果。有人拿着这个水果，可能有办法拨开各层，但就这个水果本身而言，各层虽然组成水果，但无论从哪点看来，却都是分开的。", "en": "It will be found in some important respects that the dream universe, which began even then, has somewhat the same relationships to the physical universe, but on a psychic level, that the physical universe has to the universe of negative matter. They represent skins, layers of skin, all belonging to the same fruit. Someone holding the fruit might be able to peel away the layers, but as for the fruit itself, the layers while making up the fruit are to all intents and purposes separate.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第108节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "108", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0030", "zh": "我们会从另一面往内看，因为从另一面也有一种往内看。我以前提过，梦宇宙的资料在你们的宇宙有它们的作用，在伪装之下，第五维度真的是透明的。我说过梦宇宙的资料对你们的宇宙有它的效应，就像你们的宇宙对梦宇宙也有它的效应。梦宇宙熟悉你们自己宇宙的程度，至少不下于你们熟悉它的程度，这也是真的；在你们把频率对准它之际，当你们是它的存活所需、创造它的同时，梦宇宙也把频率对准你们。你们的存活依赖着它的存活，所以如果你们从另一面看你们的宇宙，那它的确创造出你们这一个副产品。", "en": "We shall look in from the other side, for there is a looking-in also from the other side. I have mentioned before that beneath camouflage the fifth dimension is truly transparent. I have said that dream universe data has its effect upon your universe, as your universe has its effect upon the dream universe. It is also true that the dream universe is at least as familiar with your own universe as you are familiar with it; and as you tune in on it, so to speak, and while you are necessary for its survival, creating it, so does the dream universe tune in on you. So is your survival dependent upon its survival, and so does it create you as a by-product, if you are looking at your universe from the other side.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第111节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "111", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0033", "zh": "这里要牢记在心的是，虽然要等上好一阵子才会讨论，但是在梦宇宙和负物质世界之间有一种类似的关系产生。环绕在这三重系统四周的是一个，可以说，未伪装心灵现象的外壳。换句话说，就是我们很后面才会讲到的心灵能量完形。不管怎样，它们是重要的；而且从你们现在所知，你们了解到这些能量形式代表精神围场单位，运作方式和我们在讨论物质场域之内能量的早期发展时，谈到的那些较早的形式一样。", "en": "Keep in mind here, though a discussion will wait for quite a while, that a like relationship occurs between the dream universe and the world of negative matter. There is surrounding this threefold system an envelope, so to speak, of uncamouflaged psychic phenomena. In other words, psychic energy gestalts, of which we will speak much later. They are important however; and from what you now know you realize that these energy forms represent mental enclosure units, operating in the same manner as our earlier ones of which we spoke when discussing the early development of energy within the physical field.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第111节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "111", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0057", "zh": "梦宇宙、梦经验，只是另一个经验的一小部分而已。", "en": "The dream universe, the dream experience, is only a small portion of another experience.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第127节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "127", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0061", "zh": "这番话听起来可能简单到不值得一提，但是了解这番话是非常重要的事。同样的，梦宇宙和物质宇宙之间事实上也没有特定的界限或划定的界线。任何表面的界线都是人工的，因为这些实相全都一个个彼此融合在一起，而且其中一个之内的行动也都会影响另一个。", "en": "Such a remark may appear so simple that it is not worth saying, but it is extremely important that it be understood. In like manner, there is indeed no particular boundary or line of demarcation between the dream universe and the physical universe. Any seeming barrier is artificial, for all these realities merge one into the other, and an action in one affects the other.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第146节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "146", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0105", "zh": "导致世界大战的那些问题，同时也造成全球性的自然灾难。这些只不过是那些还不懂得驾驭能量的人所投射出的能量的另一些显形。这样的反应也贯穿梦境宇宙爆发出来，并在你们活动的所有阶段中被反射出来。整个自己拿它自己在物质实相与梦境实相中各个部分的表现相互比较，得出自己的结论。", "en": "Problems leading to world wars also cause worldwide natural disasters. These are merely another materialization of energy projected by those who have not learned how to handle it. Such reactions fire through the dream universe also, and are reflected through all phases of your activity. The whole self compares the performance of various portions of itself in physical reality and in dream reality, and draws its own conclusions.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第446节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "446", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0106", "zh": "在这般丰盈之中，没有一样东西是无意义的，也没有一样是被浪费的。中有相互关联，有交织缠绕的实相，有无法否认的联系。我告诉过你们，梦的实相比你们所知的更宏大，而梦的宇宙不管你们感知与否都持续着。在那个脉络之中，那些居民又依次做着他们自己的梦，形成电磁的实相。可以说，你们并不在觉知之堆的顶上，也不在底下。你们不在中心。你们也不在边沿。", "en": "In this abundance nothing is meaningless nor wasted. There is interrelationship, intertwining realities, and connections that cannot be denied. I told you that dream reality consisted of more than you knew, and that the dream universe continued whether or not you perceived it. Within that context those inhabitants dream in turn their own dreams and form electromagnetic realities. You are not at the top nor at the bottom of the heap of consciousness, so to speak. You are not at the center. You are not at the rim.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第453节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "453", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0107", "zh": "在灵视与灵感里，人们知道基督的戏剧即将演出，因此当它实质地发生时，人们就认出了它的本质。它的威力与力量然后又回到了梦的宇宙，经过物质的具体化增加了它的活力与强度。在个人的梦里，人然后再与戏中的主要人物相联系，而在梦境他们认识了它的真正重要性。", "en": "In visions and inspirations, men knew that the Christ drama would be enacted and hence recognized it for what it was when it occurred physically. Its power and strength then returned to the dream universe. It had increased its vigor and intensity through the physical materialization. In private dreams, men then related to the main figures in the drama, and in the dream state they recognized its true import.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第560节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "560", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-005-e0110", "zh": "对我而言，你们的世界是我受邀访问的梦的宇宙，一个我发现很独特而非常亲切的可能实相——却是个我不再有直接经验的实相，因我不像你们一样沉浸其中。我能告诉你它的许多事，因为你们精确的贯注必然会造成一个较狭窄而集中的视角。", "en": "To me your world is a dream universe which I visit by invitation, a probable reality that I find unique and very dear — but one in which I can no longer have direct experience. Because I am not as immersed in it as you, I can tell you much about it, since your precise orientation necessitates a more narrow, concentrated view.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第790节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "790", "only_en": true}]}]}], "reading": [], "books": [{"name": "早期课第3册", "count": 40}, {"name": "早期课第4册", "count": 23}, {"name": "灵魂永生", "count": 2}, {"name": "早期课第9册", "count": 2}, {"name": "梦、进化与价值完成", "count": 1}, {"name": "早期课第6册", "count": 1}, {"name": "心灵的本质", "count": 1}], "span": [1964, 1979], "stats": {"blocks": 8, "quotes": 70, "reading": 0, "reading_tagged": 0, "tagged": 0, "only_en": 5}};
